    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\theta=30^{\\circ},\\ 90^{\\circ},\\ 150^{\\circ}$.\n\nFactor to obtain $\\sin\\theta=\\tfrac12$ or $\\sin\\theta=1$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2\\sin^{2}\\theta-3\\sin\\theta+1&=0\\\\(2\\sin\\theta-1)(\\sin\\theta-1)&=0\\\\\\sin\\theta&=\\tfrac12\\text{ or }\\sin\\theta=1\\end{align*}$$\n\nFor $\\sin\\theta=\\tfrac12$, the related angle is $30^{\\circ}$. Sine is positive in quadrants 1 and 2.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=30^{\\circ},\\ 180^{\\circ}-30^{\\circ}\\\\\\theta&=30^{\\circ},\\ 150^{\\circ}\\end{align*}$$\n\nFor the special value $\\sin\\theta=1$, the unit circle gives:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin\\theta&=1\\\\\\theta&=90^{\\circ}\\end{align*}$$\n\nAll three values lie in the stated domain.\n\n$$\\theta=30^{\\circ},\\ 90^{\\circ},\\ 150^{\\circ}.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
